{"kind":"assert","text":"FW-1 results before the restart (hakuin.local, kit at origin main 4e5d6c87, private outputs in ~/play/artroom-private-evidence/2026-11-17-fw1). Then the owner's restart list, then one question. I stop here.\n\nResults:\n1. First room, 22:04-22:05Z, per docs/self-host-mac.md: plan (Register 28, sc_e35cnvna…), prepare-project with --application-trust-file (one row: Counter 0.3.0), deploy.py exit 0, health {\"sessions\":\"ok\"}, then PHASE=run exit 0: register installed, room created, health register \"ready\", verifiedScopes 7. Directory sc_6bafjwdf…, Membership sc_yj5qpf7c…, Rules sc_4xtvrj77…. Health now answers at https://hakuin.local (the earlier hang, 2b414302, ended with the deployment).\n2. Counter 0.3.0 install: git+https://github.com/generalbusiness-ai/dap.git/@20caa2d4a453be35e55fdeeb7ad461733db59681/apps/counter/releases/0.3.0/application.dap.json (blob d77f239f, matching the signing record), release sha256:0b3e5038…a32e1, --role admin --role member. Without --values the room refused it with bad-field (request fw1-counter-install-1). With --values '{\"target\":2}' (request fw1-counter-install-2): item 2, \"active (creation)\". Counter scope sc_zcb7yzvd…, genesis sha256:58ec967b….\n3. Counted act: initialize, participate, activate, start, commit n=1, then fulfill. The fulfill took effect at entry 7 (sha256:71c8075c…). The board shows serial 1; the promise is fulfilled.\n4. Journal read: dap verify on the Counter scope reports consistent, entries 0 to 7. dap verify --all: \"All consistent: 8 scopes\", 28 verified dependencies, 0 missing.\n5. Screen: the URL that dap application prints (https://hakuin.local/applications/\u003cdirectory\u003e/2/\u003cpresentation\u003e/) answers 404 not-found. Cause (packages/scope/src/applications/route.ts:115-126): the room's own host never serves package screens. It only redirects to an APPLICATION_SCREEN_HOSTS origin, and this project has none.\nDoc findings for the CB-1 note: Counter needs --values with its target (the guide names no values); dap act crashes with an uncaught FieldShapeError when a list field holds a nested @handle (a full member reference works).\n\nOwner commands, from docs/self-host-mac.md \"Maintain the host\", run from the fleet worktree with no gate running:\n  sudo /Library/dap-host/bin/down --prefix /Library/dap-host\n    Purpose: preserve shutdown of celld, then stop the store. Writes nothing new; data stays under /Library/dap-host/data. A nonzero exit means the result is unknown: keep everything and restart.\n  for service in seaweedfs celld caddy; do\n    sudo launchctl enable \"system/org.generalbusiness.dap.$service\"\n    sudo launchctl bootstrap system \"/Library/LaunchDaemons/org.generalbusiness.dap.$service.plist\"\n  done\n    Purpose: start the three services again, in order. Writes the launchd enable state only.\nAfter the owner reports, I run dap verify --all and the Counter journal read again, without sudo.\n\nQuestion, retained screen bytes (request step 4): without a screen host, the only place to read them is the fleet bucket under r2/application-content/, through the store's S3 endpoint on 127.0.0.1:28133. That read signs with ~/.dap-mac-aws.json. My plan: read that file only inside the signing command and print no value, list the objects under the prefix, and compare the stored packet's SHA-256 with the signed packet's 81b59b8c… before and after the restart. Do you approve this read? The alternative is a screen-host origin, which needs a second name, a certificate and a Caddy change (sudo).","body":{"to":"20db43a245e9780b92a587425d387d393b17ffc90b89e036ff752399f88fc517"}}